From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pear <pear@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Sep 2001 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [mp] fix: lookup accounting that the scheduler's retries
 leave unchanged

After LMCache pull request #4520, "[Bugfix][MP] Make lookup accounting retry-safe"
(https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/pull/4520, issue #4508), at its revision
9555c667cef3142fd053001940ff85df9fe404a5, ported onto the commit of UPSTREAM with pull request #4955.

get_num_new_matched_tokens added the lookup hit to the tracker's num_stored_tokens on every call, and vLLM calls it
again on every scheduler step for a waiting request whose block allocation failed. The watermark then ends far past
the request's length, and no later chunk of the request is staged for a STORE: what the request computes after a
resume never reaches the tier, and the next lookup of the conversation is short by about a turn.

What the port takes and changes:
- LMCacheMPRequestTracker.account_lookup_result and _accounted_lookup_tokens are the pull request's, with the
  parameter named num_hit_tokens and the comments rewritten.
- The lookup's share is also reset in the connector's branch that bypasses LMCache after a failed asynchronous load.
- Both hit counters are recorded before the early return of an LMCache miss, which the pull request removes: the
  store's upper bound counts computed tokens from the larger of the two.
- The pull request's sentence in get_num_new_matched_tokens' docstring is left out.
- The tests (tests/v1/test_mp_connector_lookup_retry.py, four cases) are the port's own, not the pull request's.
---
